    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL; load KanbanCard.tsx, KanbanCard.styles.ts, todoScoring.ts, and Grep-confirm the post-task-003 location of PriorityScoreCard/EffortScoreCard before editing.</step>
    <step order="1">Grep the repo for PriorityScoreCard.tsx / EffortScoreCard.tsx to confirm their post-hoist package path; if still under src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/... (task 003 not actually landed), STOP and escalate per the trigger below.</step>
    <step order="2">Extend the shared IKanbanCardTodo / kanban.ts types (if needed) to include sprk_priority and sprk_effort as structurally-typed optional fields.</step>
    <step order="3">Add a small priority glyph (colored dot or flag icon from @fluentui/react-icons) to KanbanCard.tsx, positioned per the existing card layout (near the score circle or title), colored via semantic tokens keyed off the priority value (e.g. Urgent/High/Medium/Low mapped to colorPaletteRed/Yellow/... foreground tokens — reuse the existing due-badge color pattern as precedent for a data-driven-but-token-based approach).</step>
    <step order="4">Add an effort indicator (e.g. a compact label or icon) to KanbanCard.tsx reflecting sprk_effort.</step>
    <step order="5">Extend PriorityScoreCard and EffortScoreCard (the detail-pane breakdown cards) to surface the new choice value alongside the existing numeric score/factor breakdown, without altering the factor-table logic.</step>
    <step order="6">Write/update unit tests for KanbanCard (glyph renders per priority/effort value; glyph absent/neutral when unset) and for PriorityScoreCard/EffortScoreCard.</step>
    <step order="7">Verify zero hex/rgb literals via grep; run npm test for the shared package.</step>
    <step order="8">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: mark 012 complete.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviation in projects/smart-todo-r5/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If task 003's hoist has not actually landed PriorityScoreCard/EffortScoreCard into @spaarke/smart-todo-components (i.e., they are still only in src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/components/SmartToDo/ at task-start), STOP and escalate rather than editing the pre-hoist LegalWorkspace-local copies — editing those would violate the Phase-1-before-Phase-2-card-UI ordering constraint (spec.md Dependencies) and get overwritten/duplicated by the hoist.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Priority/Effort Glyph Rendering">
      <steps>
        <step>Render KanbanCard with sprk_priority = each of Urgent/High/Medium/Low and sprk_effort = each of None/Very High/High/Medium/Low</step>
        <step>Verify the glyph/indicator reflects the correct value for each combination</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Each priority/effort value renders a visually distinct, correctly colored glyph/indicator; unset values render a neutral/no-op state (no crash, no misleading color).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Render KanbanCard (with a populated priority/effort glyph) in a harness with webLightTheme</step>
        <step>Switch to webDarkTheme</step>
        <step>Verify glyph/indicator colors adapt via semantic tokens with no hardcoded hex/rgb</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All glyph/indicator colors adapt correctly in both themes with zero hex/rgb literals per ADR-021.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build/test the shared lib (Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run grep for hex/rgb literal audit</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/components/KanbanCard/KanbanCard.tsx (updated)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/components/KanbanCard/KanbanCard.styles.ts (updated)</output>
    <output type="code">PriorityScoreCard + EffortScoreCard (post-hoist location, updated)</output>
    <output type="test">updated/added unit tests for the above</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a To Do with sprk_priority = Urgent/High/Medium/Low, when the KanbanCard renders, then a distinctly colored priority glyph appears matching that value.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a To Do with sprk_effort set, when the KanbanCard renders, then an effort indicator appears reflecting that value.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a To Do with sprk_priority/sprk_effort unset (null), when the KanbanCard renders, then a neutral/no-op state is shown — no crash, no misleading default color.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Zero hex/rgb literals introduced by this task (grep-verified); all new colors use Fluent v9 semantic tokens.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Light/dark theme parity holds for the new glyph/indicator (ui-test above).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new component created for this surface — PriorityScoreCard/EffortScoreCard are extended in place; all unit tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>See spec.md FR-02/FR-03 Assumptions: "assuming a Fluent v9 colored dot or flag glyph; exact icon selected during implementation." KanbanCard.tsx already has a precedent for data-driven-but-token-based coloring (due-badge urgency colors) — follow that pattern rather than inventing a new styling approach.

COMPLETION (2026-08-16): Grep-confirmed task 003's hoist had landed BOTH PriorityScoreCard.tsx and EffortScoreCard.tsx at `components/SmartToDo/` (not the POML's assumed top-level `PriorityScoreCard/`/`EffortScoreCard/` folders) — escalation trigger did not fire (files present, not still LW-local). Also discovered a SECOND live Kanban card beyond the POML's pre-hoist file list: `components/SmartToDo/KanbanCard.tsx` (the RecordCardShell-based rich card, aliased `SmartToDoKanbanCard`, consumed by the LegalWorkspace SmartToDo Code Page) — independently live alongside the POML-named widget card (`components/KanbanCard/KanbanCard.tsx`, consumed by the SpaarkeAi widget). Per the goal's "on every card" wording and FR-02's card-surface-agnostic acceptance criterion, added the priority glyph (`Flag16Filled`, 4-tier semantic-token color) + effort badge (5-tier pill) to BOTH cards, using per-file-local `derivePriorityGlyph`/`deriveEffortBadge` exports (matching each file's own pre-existing `DUE_BADGE_STYLE` duplication convention rather than introducing a new shared module). Extended `PriorityScoreCard`/`EffortScoreCard` in place with a new optional prop each (`priorityChoice`/`effortChoice`) rendering an internal, non-exported "Selected:" badge that reuses the existing `LevelBadge`/`EffortLevelBadge` tone classes (2 net-new CSS classes for the 2 choice tiers with no score-derived equivalent) — zero changes to the existing score-derived badge components' signatures or call sites (verified). `IKanbanCardTodo`/`ITodo`/`todoScoringTypes.ts` were NOT widened (out of this task's `src/components/**`-only edit scope, concurrent-agent boundary) — the two Choice fields are read via a documented local structural-type `as unknown as` cast in each KanbanCard file; recommend a fast-follow task formally add `sprk_priority`/`sprk_effort` to the shared types and remove the casts. `PriorityScoreCard`/`EffortScoreCard`'s new props are additive but not wired to their only current caller (`TodoAISummaryDialog.tsx`, which receives mock/AI-summary `ITodoScoringResult`, not a raw `ITodo`) — documented as an intentional scope boundary, not a defect. No test runner exists in this package (`tsc --noEmit` only, confirmed via package.json + no jest/vitest devDependency) — added `__tests__/priorityEffortCardUi.test.ts` following the package's existing Jest-less `assert()`-based pure-function convention (`useKanbanColumns.test.ts`/`SmartTodoWidget.test.tsx` precedent), exercising every exported mapping function across all defined Choice values + unset/out-of-range inputs; verified it type-checks cleanly via a temporary scratch tsconfig (deleted after use). `npx tsc --noEmit` exits 0. Zero hex/rgb literals (grep-verified across all 6 touched files). Full detail: `projects/smart-todo-r5/notes/task-012-card-ui.md`.</notes>

